    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0777" n="681" xml:id="pg681"/>

                <head>No. 474.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Peixotto to Mr. Hunter.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-02-06"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 6, 1872</date>.
                        (Received March 5,)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 18.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you that accounts have
                    reached here of deplorable scenes which have recently transpired in several
                    towns of Bessarabian Roumania, and especially at Ismail, Vilcovu, and
                    Cabool.</p>
                <p>The population had rushed upon the Israelites, devastated their homes, and blood
                    had been shed.</p>
                <p>Hundreds of families had been beaten, despoiled, and driven forth.</p>
                <p>Hundreds had fled across the Danube for refuge in Turkey.</p>
                <p>* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BENJ. F. PEIXOTTO,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States
                            Consul.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
